[finalize] Rebuilding quest_db.jsonl from contrib is NOT a straight key-strip: questdb ids are apostrophe-stripped/&-to-and slugs (cooks-assistant, romeo-and-juliet) while a minority are Title_Case_With_Underscores (Sheep_Herder, Wanted!->Wanted...), and classify:* titles keep punctuation -- naive slug matching reports ~39 phantom gaps. Also classify:Romeo___Juliet carries title:null (its & was eaten at key-mint time), so any title-based join must fall back to key-derived title or it silently drops the quest. And kind cannot be trusted to separate quests from miniquests: 25 miniquests live under questdb: with kind:"quest" (incl. post-classify vale-totems, identifiable only via its refs saying "(miniquest)"); the classify census is the only reliable quest/miniquest discriminator.
