## norm-q-kandarin-05 retro
Scope: 6 quests (Zogre Flesh Eaters, Sheep Herder, Tower of Life, Clock Tower, Current Affairs, Eagles' Peak), all in/near Kandarin. 159 atoms total (36+10+32+29+18+34) across 35 checkpoints, all 6 contributed fresh (no duplicate-key skips, no concurrent-dispatch collision, zero pre-existing questatoms:* keys at session start).
Fetch cost: 6 `get --section 2 --strip` calls, all fresh network fetches (0 cache hits) -- one per quest, well under the 5-get-per-quest budget; parent-pulls-children held 6/6 despite 3 of the 6 titles being flagged "verify exists" in the brief.
Coords: only Sheep Herder (4 pins) and Tower of Life (1 pin) have any {{Map}} data; the other 4 quests have zero -- consistent with the batch-to-batch variance seen in prior waves (some batches are coord-rich, most are not).
Canonical trigger for next wave: when a brief flags "verify exists -- fall back to main page" for a /Quick guide title, still try `sections` on the /Quick guide title FIRST -- it existed in all 3 flagged cases here, and the fallback instruction should be treated as a contingency, not a default.
