## norm-q-misthalin-06 retro
Scope: 6 quests (Imp Catcher, Misthalin Mystery, Rag and Bone Man I, Sheep Shearer, Shield of Arrav, The Ides of Milk), all short/early Misthalin-region quests. 92 atoms total (2+32+16+5+23+14) across 21 checkpoints, all 6 contributed fresh -- zero pre-existing questatoms:* keys at session start.
Fetch cost: 6 `sections` probes (0 false "verify exists" flags avoided by checking anyway -- Sheep Shearer's flag was a false positive, consistent with the kandarin-05/misc-08 precedent) + 8 `get --section/--strip` calls total (6 parent-Walkthrough fetches + 2 extra bare-title fetches for Shield of Arrav's transcluded Phoenix/Black Arm Gang subpages) -- well under the 5-get-per-quest budget on every quest.
Coords: zero {{Map}}/{{NPC map}} templates found in any of the 6 quests' fetched text -- a fetch-confirmed gap across the whole batch, not a shortfall.
A local python validator (idx contiguity, checkpoint start_idx resolution + monotonicity, verb enum membership, cmp enum membership, 80-char label cap, non-empty refs) ran clean on first pass (0 errors, 92 atoms across 6 rows) before any contribute call, per the og-g5/norm-q-misc-05/misc-08 precedent -- generated all 6 rows from one script rather than hand-typing JSON.
Canonical trigger for next wave: a Quick guide's plain --section 2 fetch does NOT pull in `<choose><option>{{:Page/Subpage}}</choose>` transclusion blocks (seen on Shield of Arrav) the way it reliably pulls in plain `===H3===` nested children -- if a fetched section's prose visibly stops mid-branch-description with a `<choose>` tag instead of continuing into real checklist bullets, treat it as a signal to fetch the two (or more) transcluded subpage titles directly as their own bare-title gets, same discipline as the "parent-pulls-children" pattern but for transclusion rather than nesting.
