## norm-q-varlamore-03 retro
Scope: 5 quests (Death on the Isle, Scrambled, Vale Totems (miniquest), The Ribbiting Tale of a Lily Pad Labour Dispute, At First Light), all Varlamore-region. 133 atoms total (39+42+12+15+25) across 24 checkpoints, all 5 contributed fresh (zero pre-existing questatoms:* keys at session start, zero duplicate-key skips).
Two of five brief-flagged "verify exists" quick guides turned out NOT to be standalone pages: Scrambled/Quick guide is a straight-up 404 (used main page's Walkthrough instead), and Vale Totems (miniquest)/Quick guide is a same-title redirect back to the main page (not a distinct URL) -- both fallbacks worked cleanly with zero content loss since the target pages' Walkthrough sections were complete either way.
4 of 5 quests have zero {{Map}} templates; only At First Light carries real pin data (3 named pins, all within the surface envelope), reused across every atom at that location rather than duplicated per-atom guesswork.
Canonical trigger for next wave: when a brief flags "verify exists -- fall back to main page" for a /Quick guide title, budget one extra `sections` call up front for BOTH the quick-guide AND the plain title before any `get`, since a same-title redirect (Vale Totems) reads differently in manifest.jsonl (title/url silently drop the suffix) than a hard 404 (Scrambled) -- distinguishing the two up front avoids a wasted get attempt on a title that will 404.
No verb-enum primitives were newly needed this batch; all content mapped cleanly onto talk-to/walk-to/gather/kill/use-on/claim/equip/toggle/produce/buy per prior precedents (investigate->talk-to, pickpocket->gather).
[normalize-q] norm-q-varlamore-02: all 3 quests (Meat and Greet, Shadows of Custodia, The Heart of Darkness) have real, populated /Quick guide Walkthrough sections fetched in one get --section 2 each -- Meat and Greet/Shadows of Custodia are flat single-section checklists (1417B/1623B), The Heart of Darkness's stub Walkthrough H2 (17B listed) parent-pulled all 8 nested trial/dungeon subsections inline (7094B), extending the parent-pulls-children pattern to a GM-tier quest where -- unlike several prior batches -- NO child subsection (s3-s10) is separately manifest-recorded, so every atom cites the coarse .s2 slug since no finer one exists to prefer.
[normalize-q] norm-q-varlamore-02: The Heart of Darkness has four genuine player-randomised puzzle states in one quest (First Trial sw-chest keyword + nw-chest code, Statue Puzzle mural activation order, Third Trial cultist-traitor identity) -- all modelled as until:{"state":"??"} per the Tree Gnome Village ballista-code/Movario precedent, while the two FIXED reference tables used to derive those secrets (Takam/Makt/Silam/Uitt word-to-direction; Zema/Oma/Yeya/Naui mural-name-to-number) are literal wiki game text, not secrets, and were kept verbatim-in-spirit in atom detail -- worth distinguishing "the lookup table is public, only the per-player output is ??" from a blanket ?? on the whole mechanic.
[normalize-q] norm-q-varlamore-02: Shadows of Custodia's "Talk to Francis or Aemilia" (either-parent, no stated preference) recurs 4 separate times across the walkthrough -- modelled each occurrence as its own atom with 2 branch hints (not collapsed into one atom, not unrolled into parallel chains) per the Hazeel Cult/Murder Mystery branch precedent, since it is a real per-occurrence dialogue step each time, just with an unconstrained target choice.
[normalize-q] norm-q-varlamore-02: Meat and Greet's "give the test kebab to Vincens, Renata, or Lucas outside" is a genuine any-of-three choice with no verb-enum fit for "give" (mapped to use-on, verb-gap hint) -- modelled as ONE atom with 3 branch hints rather than 3 parallel give-atoms, extending the either-parent 2-way branch pattern to a 3-way NPC choice.
[normalize-q] norm-q-varlamore-02: dropped The Heart of Darkness's "Recommended: build the Unbuilt Landing Site in Salvager Overlook" aside and its recommended-gear/empty-inventory-slot-count lines entirely (not even as hints) -- optional, non-required-for-completion asides with no dedicated verb-enum fit, extending the Murder Mystery "drop the silver necklace" optional-aside exclusion precedent (gotcha #135) from a single quest to a GM-tier multi-trial one; flagged the omission in the row's own notes.
## norm-q-varlamore-02 retro
Scope: 3 Varlamore quests (Meat and Greet, Shadows of Custodia, The Heart of Darkness), a small-count/high-density batch (17+26+61 = 104 atoms across 17 checkpoints). Zero pre-existing questatoms:* keys at session start (checked contrib.jsonl before any fetch).
Fetch cost: 3 sections probes + 3 get --section 2 --strip calls (1 cache hit on Meat and Greet, 2 fresh on Shadows of Custodia/Heart of Darkness) -- well under the 5-get-per-quest budget on all 3, Heart of Darkness's single fetch covering its entire 8-checkpoint GM-tier walkthrough.
Coords: zero {{Map}}/{{NPC map}} templates found across all 3 quests' fetched text -- a fetch-confirmed gap, not a shortfall, matching several prior misc-* batches. Zero Grand Exchange mentions across all 3 (willow longbows for Shadows of Custodia are an NPC-shop buy from Renu, not GE, correctly non-violating).
A local python schema validator (idx contiguity, checkpoint start_idx resolution + monotonicity, verb/cmp enum membership, 80-char label cap, non-empty refs, hint-type sanity) ran clean on first pass across all 3 rows/104 atoms before any contribute call, per the established og-g5/norm-q-misc-05/misc-08 precedent.
Canonical trigger for next wave: when a stub parent-Walkthrough section pulls all its children inline (byte count matches sum-of-children), always grep manifest.jsonl for the individual child slugs BEFORE assuming they're separately citable -- Heart of Darkness is the first quest in this whole normalize-q track where the parent-pull pattern held but the fine-grained child slugs were genuinely absent from manifest (no prior session had section-fanned this specific page), so the coarse .s2 slug was the correct citation, not a shortcut taken under budget pressure.
